{"id": "EUVD-2026-80786", "enisaUuid": "b72885a9-e9ca-382e-8494-cf2f1e03b3a2", "description": "In a query response, an attacker may send `named` multiple copies of a record that should only exist once (such as an SOA record). If the RDATA is the same on all the copies, the record is appended to the in-memory RDATA set, which can cause increased memory usage of the negative cache and possibly lead to other memory attack vectors.\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.11.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.27, 9.21.0 through 9.21.25, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.27-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T14:15:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T18:40:16", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-75029", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.29", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.26"], "aliases": ["GHSA-crh2-6h8j-h25c", "CVE-2026-75029"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.48, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0528414c-7970-38ca-ba4b-656e57e26cc4", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.27"}, {"id": "1c908aae-50c3-3b61-97f5-5d2af0f57f1c", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.27-S1"}, {"id": "58e2e60d-9f15-31ac-b76f-185897f66b8e", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.0 \u22649.18.50"}, {"id": "e9f8ba13-693e-359f-8f45-434c3a01061f", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.25"}, {"id": "f1d917c8-4062-395f-8d80-b8e78c10b39a", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "32530a22-6a5a-38c6-a53c-1401b7387747", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}